{title: 499 - What a Friend We Have in Jesus}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]What a friend we have in [Bb]Jesus,
[F]All our sins and griefs to [C]bear!
[F]What a privilege to [Bb]carry
[F]Every[C7]thing to God in [F]prayer!
[C]O what peace we [C7]often [F]forfeit,
[Bb]O what [F]needless pain we [C]bear,
[F]All because we do not [Bb]carry
[F]Every[C7]thing to God in [F]prayer!

Verse 2:
[F]Have we [Bb]trials and temptations?
[F]Is there [C]trouble anywhere?
[F]We should [Bb]never be discouraged
[F]Take it [C7]to the [F]Lord in prayer.
[C]Can we [C7]find a [F]friend so faithful
[Bb]Who will [F]all our [C]sorrows share?
[F]Jesus knows [Bb]our every weakness
[F]Take it [C7]to the [F]Lord in prayer.

Verse 3:
[F]Are we weak [Bb]and heavy laden,
[F]Cumbered with a [C]load of care?
[F]Precious Savior, [Bb]still our refuge
[F]Take it [C7]to the [F]Lord in prayer.
[C]Do your [C7]friends despise, [F]forsake you?
[Bb]Take it [F]to the [C]Lord in prayer.
[F]In his arms he'll [Bb]take and shield you;
[F]You will [C7]find a [F]solace there.
